/**
 * One named sidebar per top-level topic, instead of a single sidebar
 * autogenerated from the whole docs/ tree. Pairing this with the navbar's
 * "Topics" dropdown (docusaurus.config.js) is what lets a reader pick a
 * topic at the top and see only that topic's pages in the sidebar,
 * instead of every topic in the notebook at once.
 *
 * Each sidebar is a single category wrapping the topic's own pages,
 * with `collapsed: false` so those pages are visible immediately rather
 * than needing an extra click to expand — and `link: generated-index` so
 * selecting the topic from the navbar lands on a plain Contents page for
 * it (styled by src/theme/DocCategoryGeneratedIndexPage), instead of
 * dropping straight into one arbitrary first doc.
 */

